WEBVTT

00:00:00.547 --> 00:00:02.764
Founders hire me to take products

00:00:02.764 --> 00:00:04.633
from prototype to production.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.453
This is Pulseboard,

00:00:06.471 --> 00:00:08.275
an operations dashboard for

00:00:08.275 --> 00:00:09.908
multi-location clinics.

00:00:11.507 --> 00:00:13.182
Change the date range or the

00:00:13.182 --> 00:00:15.328
locations, and every number

00:00:15.328 --> 00:00:17.279
and chart updates together.

00:00:17.813 --> 00:00:19.653
Filters live in the URL,

00:00:19.653 --> 00:00:21.651
so any view is shareable.

00:00:22.447 --> 00:00:24.287
The calls log holds nearly

00:00:24.287 --> 00:00:26.131
seventeen thousand records.

00:00:26.642 --> 00:00:29.048
Search and status filters respond

00:00:29.048 --> 00:00:29.938
instantly.

00:00:31.137 --> 00:00:32.989
Locations compares offices

00:00:32.989 --> 00:00:35.276
side by side: answer rate,

00:00:35.276 --> 00:00:37.605
no-shows, ratings and revenue.

00:00:38.497 --> 00:00:40.113
I design for failure,

00:00:40.113 --> 00:00:42.787
too. Flip the mock API into

00:00:42.787 --> 00:00:43.901
a full outage,

00:00:43.966 --> 00:00:45.428
and the app keeps the last

00:00:45.428 --> 00:00:46.619
loaded values,

00:00:46.619 --> 00:00:48.429
with clear retry paths.

00:00:49.227 --> 00:00:51.220
The same table renders fifty-five

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.299
thousand rows,

00:00:52.352 --> 00:00:54.050
while keeping only a couple

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:55.914
of dozen in the DOM,

00:00:55.914 --> 00:00:57.699
so scrolling stays smooth.

00:00:59.897 --> 00:01:00.947
A dark theme,

00:01:00.947 --> 00:01:02.704
a tested design system,

00:01:02.704 --> 00:01:04.343
and documented architecture

00:01:04.343 --> 00:01:06.993
decisions. Built to hand over

00:01:06.993 --> 00:01:08.107
to your team.

00:01:09.107 --> 00:01:10.161
I'm Ashwani,

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.926
a contract founding engineer

00:01:11.926 --> 00:01:13.464
for EU startups.

00:01:13.986 --> 00:01:15.347
Let's build yours.
